BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.090 0.196 0.302 rg 1 0 0 1 56.00 555.88 Tm (authentication service rotates refresh tokens and revokes the previous token when issuing a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.090 0.196 0.302 rg 1 0 0 1 56.00 543.28 Tm (replacement. Its lockout logic applies after five failed login attempts, with a 15-minute lock duration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.090 0.196 0.302 rg 1 0 0 1 56.00 530.68 Tm (defined in the service. Logout revokes the supplied refresh token; this should not be described as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.090 0.196 0.302 rg 1 0 0 1 56.00 518.08 Tm (immediate revocation of every previously issued access token.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.090 0.196 0.302 rg 1 0 0 1 56.00 499.48 Tm (Role and permission checks control operations, while the employee access service distinguishes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.090 0.196 0.302 rg 1 0 0 1 56.00 486.88 Tm (directory visibility, full-profile access, and sensitive-field access. Selected identifiers, including PAN,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.090 0.196 0.302 rg 1 0 0 1 56.00 474.28 Tm (Aadhaar, and bank account values, use an AES-GCM attribute converter. Masking supports ordinary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.090 0.196 0.302 rg 1 0 0 1 56.00 461.68 Tm (viewing, and sensitive reveal actions have audit coverage. These mechanisms apply to selected fields) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.090 0.196 0.302 rg 1 0 0 1 56.00 449.08 Tm (rather than proving encryption of every database column or uploaded file.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.090 0.196 0.302 rg 1 0 0 1 56.00 430.48 Tm (Uploaded files use generated UUID storage keys, a content-type allow-list, signature checks, and) Tj ET
